<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ui version="4.0">
 <class>ExtendedSliderUi</class>
 <widget class="QWidget" name="ExtendedSliderUi">
  <property name="geometry">
   <rect>
    <x>0</x>
    <y>0</y>
    <width>519</width>
    <height>138</height>
   </rect>
  </property>
  <property name="windowTitle">
   <string>Form</string>
  </property>
  <!--
    Eighteen of these stack up in the tool dock (three in Raise/Lower alone), so the layout
    metrics here are what decide how much of the panel is chrome. Four things were costing
    height or legibility for nothing.

    First, every layout took the Fusion defaults (9px margins, 6px spacing). A control that is
    already inside a group box, itself inside a panel, does not need a third 9px inset; the
    parent supplies the gutter. Margins are zeroed and the row gap is set explicitly.

    Second, the slider and the pressure bar each sat in their own single item QHBoxLayout.
    Those wrappers were pure overhead, and the pressureBar one was actively harmful: the bar is
    hidden unless a tablet is driving the value (see ExtendedSlider.cpp), and while Qt skips a
    hidden WIDGET in a layout, a nested LAYOUT holding it is not empty, so it kept claiming its
    margins and spacing on every one of the eighteen instances. Both widgets are now direct
    children of the vertical layout, which makes the hidden bar genuinely free.

    Third, the slider took whatever height the style's slider thickness happened to be - around
    22px under Fusion, and none of it used. The theme draws a 6px groove with a 16px handle
    (margin -5px top and bottom on a 6px groove is exactly 16px of handle), so 16px is the band.
    It is pinned as a MINIMUM as well as a maximum, so the row height is this file's decision
    rather than the style's and the handle cannot be clipped if a theme thickens it. That is the
    single biggest saving on the panel: ~6px x 18 instances, before the row gap below drops from
    3 to 2.

    THE BAND WAS BRIEFLY 20px AND THAT WAS A REGRESSION, NOW REVERTED. The argument for widening
    it was that the band, not the sheet, sets the hit target - that Qt derives the
    SC_SliderHandle rect from the WIDGET's height - so that at 16px the top and bottom rows of
    the grip a user can SEE would page-step instead of drag. That is true of an UNSTYLED slider
    and false of this one. Re-measured with a standalone Qt 5.15.2 probe that loads the shipped
    sheet, puts a 212px slider at 50 percent, and sweeps the pointer pixel by pixel over the
    whole control counting the positions QStyle::hitTestComplexControl(CC_Slider, ...) reports
    as SC_SliderHandle - which is the exact call QSlider::mousePressEvent uses to choose between
    starting a drag and page-stepping:

      sheet                    band   handle rect       pixels that GRAB the handle
      6px tick, 4px groove      16     6x16 @(103,0)     96 =  6 x 16
      16px grip, 6px groove     14    16x16 @(98,-1)    224 = 16 x 14  (grip clipped by band)
      16px grip, 6px groove     16    16x16 @(98,0)     256 = 16 x 16  (this file)
      16px grip, 6px groove     18    16x16 @(98,1)     256 = 16 x 16
      16px grip, 6px groove     20    16x16 @(98,2)     256 = 16 x 16
      16px grip, 6px groove     22    16x16 @(98,3)     256 = 16 x 16
      none, QWindowsVistaStyle  16    16x16 @(98,0)     256 = 16 x 16
      none, QWindowsVistaStyle  20    16x20 @(98,0)     320 = 16 x 20

    With a sheet loaded QStyleSheetStyle sizes the handle from the QSS box - 6px groove plus the
    -5px margins - and CENTRES it in the band, so the handle rect is 16x16 at every band from 16
    upwards and the widening bought exactly zero grabbable pixels. Only the last two rows, with
    no sheet at all, behave the way the widening assumed; this application always has one. So 16
    is the smallest band that does not clip the grip, and at 16 every pixel of the grip that is
    drawn also grabs it. 20 instead added four rows where a click JUMPS the value, inside the
    grip's own row, on the control that sets brush radius and speed - and charged 4px x 18
    instances for it.

    What did move the hit target is the theme's grip rewrite, from 6x16 = 96 to 16x16 = 256
    (2.7x), measured in the first two lines above. It did that without this file changing at all.

    Fourth, the value was left-aligned, so in a column of three sliders the digits started at
    three different x positions and the eye had nothing to scan down. The spinbox is now
    right-aligned. That is the whole fix and it costs no width: the row is label, expanding
    spacer, spinbox, fixed-width button, so the RIGHT edge of every spinbox in a column is
    already flush regardless of how wide each spinbox is, and right-aligned text puts the digits
    on that shared edge. A minimum width was tried here first and does not work - the spinbox
    size hints are 89px at max 1000, 95px at max 10000 and 71px at max 1, so any floor small
    enough to fit the 250px dock is below the widest of them and aligns nothing. Alignment does
    not touch the range, the step, the decimals or the emitted value.

    The pencil button is the tablet-pressure menu, NOT a mask or curve picker - read
    ExtendedSlider.cpp, the popup it opens holds "Use Tablet" and a sensitivity slider. It had
    no tooltip at all, which is most of why it reads as mysterious. It is now flat (the theme's
    QPushButton:flat is transparent until hovered) so it stops carrying the same visual weight
    as the number beside it, and 20px rather than 22px so it fits the 16px-min-height row band.

    No widget was renamed, removed or reordered; ExtendedSlider.cpp addresses the same five
    objects and none of its ranges or connections changed.
  -->
  <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="verticalLayout">
   <property name="spacing">
    <number>2</number>
   </property>
   <property name="leftMargin">
    <number>0</number>
   </property>
   <property name="topMargin">
    <number>0</number>
   </property>
   <property name="rightMargin">
    <number>0</number>
   </property>
   <property name="bottomMargin">
    <number>0</number>
   </property>
   <item>
    <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="horizontalLayout">
     <property name="spacing">
      <number>6</number>
     </property>
     <property name="leftMargin">
      <number>0</number>
     </property>
     <property name="topMargin">
      <number>0</number>
     </property>
     <property name="rightMargin">
      <number>0</number>
     </property>
     <property name="bottomMargin">
      <number>0</number>
     </property>
     <item>
      <widget class="QLabel" name="label">
       <property name="text">
        <string>Name:</string>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item>
      <spacer name="horizontalSpacer">
       <property name="orientation">
        <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
       </property>
       <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
        <size>
         <width>40</width>
         <height>20</height>
        </size>
       </property>
      </spacer>
     </item>
     <item>
      <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="doubleSpinBox">
       <property name="alignment">
        <set>Qt::AlignRight|Qt::AlignTrailing|Qt::AlignVCenter</set>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item>
      <widget class="QPushButton" name="tabletControlMenuButton">
       <property name="sizePolicy">
        <sizepolicy hsizetype="Fixed" vsizetype="Fixed">
         <horstretch>0</horstretch>
         <verstretch>0</verstretch>
        </sizepolicy>
       </property>
       <property name="minimumSize">
        <size>
         <width>20</width>
         <height>20</height>
        </size>
       </property>
       <property name="maximumSize">
        <size>
         <width>20</width>
         <height>20</height>
        </size>
       </property>
       <property name="text">
        <string/>
       </property>
       <property name="flat">
        <bool>true</bool>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
    </layout>
   </item>
   <item>
    <widget class="QSlider" name="slider">
     <property name="minimumSize">
      <size>
       <width>0</width>
       <height>16</height>
      </size>
     </property>
     <property name="maximumSize">
      <size>
       <width>16777215</width>
       <height>16</height>
      </size>
     </property>
     <property name="orientation">
      <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
    <widget class="QProgressBar" name="pressureBar">
     <property name="maximumSize">
      <size>
       <width>16777215</width>
       <height>4</height>
      </size>
     </property>
     <property name="value">
      <number>0</number>
     </property>
     <property name="textVisible">
